strptime as POSIX says (libc-test's functional/strptime): %c, %x and
%X read the locale's formats, %E and %O modifiers are taken, %n and %t
take any white space, none included, %U, %W, %V, %g and %G are read,
%z takes Z and +hh, +hhmm and +hh:mm, %Z a zone name, and %s seconds
since the Epoch. mlibc's aborted the program on most of these. Meant
for upstream.

